Now we need to manage operational constraints: we have two: alpha and beta. Each shift candidate has candidate_operational_constraint_linked to respective constraint. So we need to apply operational_constraint_alpha for shift_candidate_alpha, and operational_constraint_beta for shift_candidate_beta.

Compliance certificate: only one compliance_certificate_alpha. Both shift candidates have candidate_compliance_certificate_linked to compliance_certificate_alpha in init. So after we assign to shift alpha, it becomes unavailable; we need to release before assigning to shift beta. There's action release_compliance_certificate. So we need to release after use.

Similarly skill certificate not needed.

Equipment resources: not needed for schedule candidates via compliance path; we can skip.

Now we need to ensure we don't violate negative preconditions: e.g., not (dispatched ?candidate) etc.

